  "id": "information-test",
  "term": "information test",
  "definition": "An information test, as supported here by the concealed information test, is a method used to detect whether a person has knowledge they are trying to hide. It does this by looking for behavioral or physiological signs, such as changes in reaction time, that may reveal concealed knowledge.",
